# Environment variables for the local Docker Compose stack (ticket 07).
#
# Usage: `cp .env.example .env`, then `docker compose up --build`.
# `.env` itself is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# IMPORTANT for future tickets: every new backend/frontend env var must be
# added here (with a comment) when it is introduced — this file must always
# document every variable the compose stack needs at that point in time.
# docker-compose.yml already forwards the whole file to the backend
# container via `env_file`, so most new backend variables need no
# docker-compose.yml change, only a new line here.

# ---- Reverse proxy ----

# Host port the whole stack is reachable on once `docker compose up` is
# running:
#   http://localhost:${PROXY_PORT}/         -> frontend widget
#   http://localhost:${PROXY_PORT}/health   -> backend health check
#   http://localhost:${PROXY_PORT}/api/...  -> backend API
PROXY_PORT=8080

# ---- Backend (app/core/config.py) ----

# Optional overrides for the config-driven registries. Defaults already
# match the paths baked into the backend image by backend/Dockerfile, so
# these normally do not need to be set — uncomment only to point the
# container at a different mounted config file.
# NAKS_TEMPLATE_REGISTRY_PATH=/app/config/templates.yaml
# NAKS_AC_REGISTRY_PATH=/app/config/attestation_centers.yaml
# NAKS_WARNING_RULES_PATH=/app/config/warning_rules.yaml

# ---- LLM provider (ticket 04) ----

# Which LLMProvider implementation to build at startup, by name.
#   mock       — deterministic fixtures, no vendor account, no network.
#   anthropic  — real calls to the Anthropic API.
#
# An unknown name, or a real provider whose credentials are missing, stops the
# app at startup with an explicit message. There is deliberately no silent
# fallback to `mock`: running without a vendor is supported, but has to be
# chosen here rather than happening by accident.
NAKS_LLM_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only when NAKS_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic. Unprefixed on purpose — it
# is the name the vendor's own SDK and docs use.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional override of the model used by the anthropic provider.
# NAKS_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Rate-limiting config (ticket 06) must be appended above when it lands.

# ---- Frontend / iframe embedding (ticket 05) ----

# Comma-separated list of host page origins the widget will exchange
# postMessage with, e.g.
#   WIDGET_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS=https://ac.example,https://partner.example
#
# Empty (the default) means same-origin only, which is what the bundled demo
# page at http://localhost:${PROXY_PORT}/embed-demo.html uses. A host that is
# not listed here gets nothing: the widget never posts to "*".
#
# NOTE — this does NOT restrict who may frame the widget. It governs the
# postMessage conversation only: an unlisted site can still put the widget in
# an iframe, it just gets no auto-resize. Framing is not something a bundle
# can control; restricting it needs a `Content-Security-Policy:
# frame-ancestors` (or X-Frame-Options) header from whatever serves the
# widget, and neither nginx config sets one today. Worth adding before any
# real deployment — a page nobody vetted can otherwise frame the widget under
# its own branding. (It cannot read what users type: cross-origin iframes are
# isolated, so the risk is clickjacking and impersonation, not data theft.)
#
# NOTE: this one is build-time, not runtime — Vite inlines it into the bundle.
# After changing it run `docker compose build frontend` (a plain restart will
# not pick it up).
WIDGET_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS=
